# Optional local overrides for development and VM test targets.
# Process env always wins over .env. This file is gitignored when named `.env`.
#
# Preferred local setup: in 1Password desktop, mount an Environment at this path
# (Developer → Environments → local .env). That mount is a FIFO; do not replace
# it with a plaintext file if you want 1Password to keep managing it.
#
# Headless SDK bootstrap (only needed when the local .env is incomplete):
# OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID=envs/...
# OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=ops_...   # full token; must start with ops_
# OP_ACCOUNT=my.1password.account    # alternative to service account token
#
# Usage billing. Mode defaults to shadow (statements and dry-run
# restrictions; never charges). Enabled mode requires Stripe keys and a
# completed shadow period first. See docs/billing.md.
# CONTROLPLANE_BILLING_MODE=shadow
# CONTROLPLANE_BILLING_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
# CONTROLPLANE_BILLING_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# CONTROLPLANE_BILLING_CHECKOUT_SUCCESS_URL=https://console.example.test/workspace/billing/checkout/success
# CONTROLPLANE_BILLING_CHECKOUT_CANCEL_URL=https://console.example.test/workspace/billing/checkout/cancel
# Stripe webhook endpoint: https://console.example.test/webhooks/stripe
# Feature keys can also live here directly:
# CONTROLPLANE_GITHUB_APP_ID=...
# CONTROLPLANE_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...
# CONTROLPLANE_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=...
# For standalone control-plane deployments. localteststack supplies these and
# starts an authenticated registry automatically.
# CONTROLPLANE_REGISTRY_HOST=...
# CONTROLPLANE_REGISTRY_AUTH_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9444
# CONTROLPLANE_REGISTRY_TOKEN_ISSUER=ebpf-wg-mesh
# CONTROLPLANE_REGISTRY_TOKEN_SERVICE=registry.example.test
# CONTROLPLANE_REGISTRY_CREDENTIAL_TTL_SECONDS=300
# Optional persistent override; defaults to CONTROLPLANE_STATE_DIR/pki/revoked-client-cert-serials.txt:
# Certificate revocations are stored in the shared platform database.
# Source snapshots: file and S3 work in production. File storage needs a persistent absolute
# path, defaults under CONTROLPLANE_STATE_DIR, and an off-machine backup. Optional S3:
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_PROVIDER=s3
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_BUCKET=platform-source-archives
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_PREFIX=snapshots
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_SSE=AES256
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_KMS_KEY_ID=arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:1234:key/abcd
# Credentials: JSON file with access_key_id/secret_access_key, or empty for
# environment / container / instance workload identity:
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/etc/ebpf-wg-mesh/s3-credentials.json
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_S3_MAX_RETRIES=3
# CONTROLPLANE_SOURCE_ARCHIVES_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Use the same distinct 32+ byte value for both assertion settings:
# CONTROLPLANE_USER_ASSERTION_SECRET=...
# DASHBOARD_CONTROLPLANE_USER_ASSERTION_SECRET=...
# Envelope master keys for service env and signing keys. Development bootstraps the default file
# (CONTROLPLANE_STATE_DIR/secret-keys/keys.json) automatically; production
# requires the operator to provision the same keyring file to every replica.
# CONTROLPLANE_SECRET_KEYS_KEYRING=/etc/ebpf-wg-mesh/secret-keys/keys.json
# xDS management API for Envoy. Loopback by default; production requires an
# explicit host. mTLS is required, so keep the listener network-isolated as well.
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_XDS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:18000
# Automatic HTTPS. Production defaults to Let's Encrypt and issues one certificate per
# public hostname over HTTP-01, so the CA must reach an Envoy HTTP listener on port 80.
# Development leaves it off unless a directory is set.
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_HTTP_LISTEN=:80
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_HTTPS_LISTEN=:443
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_ACME_DIRECTORY_URL=https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_ACME_EMAIL=ops@example.com
# Optional wildcard certificate for *.<CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_PUBLIC_ADDR>; generated hostnames
# use it instead of per-hostname certificates, which keeps clear of CA rate limits.
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_PLATFORM_TLS_CERT_FILE=/etc/ebpf-wg-mesh/tls/platform.crt
# CONTROLPLANE_INGRESS_PLATFORM_TLS_KEY_FILE=/etc/ebpf-wg-mesh/tls/platform.key
# DASHBOARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=...
# DASHBOARD_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=...
# DASHBOARD_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# The matching GitHub login receives fleet operator access in `make dev-ephemeral`.
# LOCALTESTSTACK_OPERATOR_GITHUB_LOGIN=your-github-username
# Required for every dashboard; generate independently with `openssl rand -base64 32`:
# DASHBOARD_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=...
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=...
# CLOUDFLARE_HOSTNAME=...
#
# Hetzner Cloud token for production-replica VM smoke (`make test-e2e-vm`):
# HCLOUD_TOKEN=...
# Optional on independently provisioned agents; defaults from the advertised host address.
# AGENT_MESH_ADVERTISE_ENDPOINT=[2001:db8::10]:51820

# OVH disposable stress fixture (also accepts an ignored .env.ovh file).
# API credentials belong to one endpoint; this is independent of VM region.
# OVH_ENDPOINT=ovh-ca
# OVH_APPLICATION_KEY=...
# OVH_APPLICATION_SECRET=...
# OVH_CONSUMER_KEY=...
# OVH_CLOUD_PROJECT=...

# Telemetry (all Go components; see docs/observability.md). Deployments inject
# these automatically when the optional observability roles are enabled. For an
# external backend, point OTLP at it and scrape TELEMETRY_METRICS_LISTEN.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=collector-host:4317
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE=true
# TELEMETRY_METRICS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9095
# TELEMETRY_METRICS_TOKEN=...
# TELEMETRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATIO=1
# TELEMETRY_LOG_FORMAT=json
# TELEMETRY_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Public API (REST/JSON under /v1; loopback plaintext, expose behind TLS).
# CONTROLPLANE_PUBLIC_API_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9445
# CONTROLPLANE_PUBLIC_API_RPH=10000
# CONTROLPLANE_PUBLIC_API_RPS=50
# MCP server (cmd/mcp). PLATFORM_API_TOKEN is a wgm_ API token secret;
# create one with `controlplane api-token create` or the dashboard RPCs.
# PLATFORM_API_URL=https://api.example.test
# PLATFORM_API_TOKEN=wgm_...
# PLATFORM_WORKSPACE_ID=...  # linked defaults for MCP tools
# PLATFORM_PROJECT_ID=...
# PLATFORM_ENVIRONMENT_ID=...
# PLATFORM_SERVICE_ID=...
# Remote MCP (platform-mcp --http):
# MCP_HTTP_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080
# MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://mcp.example.test/mcp
